  1049	// TestSemanticIndexNoOpsWhenIndexIsAlreadyCurrent replaces
  1050	// TestSemanticIndexRequiresForceWhenIndexExists, which pinned the behaviour
  1051	// that made the documented refresh sequence fail on every run after the first:
  1052	// a second `refresh index` exited 1 purely because an index existed, while its
  1053	// parent `refresh` was idempotent and exited 0.
  1054	//
  1055	// The contract is now the one a scripted loop can use. Already current is a
  1056	// no-op that succeeds and says so; --force still rebuilds unconditionally. The
  1057	// cases that make a re-run do real work (stale commit, unreadable store) are
  1058	// pinned in honest_reporting_fixes_test.go.
  1059	func TestSemanticIndexNoOpsWhenIndexIsAlreadyCurrent(t *testing.T) {
